   <media:title>One Wisconsin. On Wisconsin: Strengthening EMS systems across the state</media:title>
   <media:content url="https://www.youtube.com/v/FniAHDK3cpY?version=3" type="application/x-shockwave-flash" width="640" height="390"/>
   <media:thumbnail url="https://i3.ytimg.com/vi/FniAHDK3cpY/hqdefault.jpg" width="480" height="360"/>
   <media:description>Housed within the University of Wisconsin School of Medicine and Public Health, the Wisconsin Office of Rural Health (WORH) offers a wide range of services aimed at improving health outcomes in the state’s rural communities.  Emergency medical services are coming under strain due to workforce shortages and rising costs. WORH, in partnership with local elected officials in Vilas County, created a new EMS district that’s cut response times in half.  

Featuring:
Lori Scarcelli, Communications Lieutenant at the Vilas County Sheriff’s Office
John Hanson, Manitowish Waters Town Chair
James Small, rural EMS outreach manager at Wisconsin Office of Rural Health
Jason Joling,  Chief of the Northwoods EMS District</media:description>
